& [CatalogueContract] is immutable and content bound
  + [principal_identity] is cantor-in-memory-catalogue/0.1
  + empty, inserted, suspended, revoked, and superseded catalogues are digest-bound values
  + insertion requires exact active admission, compiled procedure digest, reciprocal aliases, and valid predecessor generation
  + accepted insertion returns evidence-rich receipt plus one successor value
  + refused insertion returns evidence-rich receipt and no successor
  + lookup returns exact version, procedure digest, admission identity and digest, status, aliases, and revocation identity
  + revocation preserves entries, aliases, prior generations, receipts, and exact record lineage

& [InterpreterContract] is deterministic bounded local execution
  + [interpreter_identity] is cantor-effectless-interpreter/0.1
  + invocation requires exact active catalogue, procedure, admission, schema set, anchor set, policy, request, and budget bindings before the first step
  + bind, inspect, compare, branch, select, bounded identity map, return, and fault operate over immutable successor states
  + at most one instruction is evaluated per step with stable region and instruction identity
  + result includes typed output or fault, final state, exact process steps, digest-bound causal trace, consumed budget, residuals, proof refs, sensitivity, and retention
  + malformed operand contracts, stale inputs, resource exhaustion, and schema mismatch return typed results rather than partial success
  + identical catalogue, IR, admission, and request inputs produce byte-equivalent output

& [CoordinationBoundary] is explicit
  + Emit, Receive, Yield, WaitLogical, Reactivate, Join, and multi-process scheduling return typed CPPE-I06 residuals
  + coordination operators are recognized and never silently simulated by the local interpreter
  + no shared hidden state, thread, physical clock, message transport, provider, persistence, or external effect is present

& [ReviewCorrections] are incorporated
  + consumed step and logical-time totals derive from executed steps rather than trace-event count
  + a faulting ProcessStep and returned ProcedureFault share one exact fault identity
  + catalogue receipts carry evidence, diagnostics, and safe residuals
  + aggregate validation checks catalogue, receipt, trace, request, result, alias, revocation, and causal predecessor identities
  + instruction operand faults become typed InvocationResult faults instead of host errors

& [AuthoritySeparation] is explicit
  + catalogue insertion does not invoke and invocation does not mutate the catalogue
  + deterministic execution proves repeatability only, not truth, universal safety, fitness, consent, or effect authority
  + no textual parser, live provider, persistence, service, model execution, external process, network, filesystem, database, hardware, or FPGA surface is present

& [SolutionDisposition] is accepted for CPPE-I05 after completed-work review
  + [next] separately claim CPPE-I06 after commit and push
